{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>וימת שם משה.</b> Is it possible that Moses died and then wrote <b>וימת שם משה</b>? Rather, up to here Moses wrote; from here onward Joshua wrote. Rabbi Meir says: Is it possible that the Book of the Torah is missing anything, when it says ״לָקֹחַ אֵת סֵפֶר הַתּוֹרָה הַזֶּה״ (Deuteronomy 31)? Rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, speaks and Moses writes in tears. (Sifrei; Bava Batra 15a, Menachot 30a)" "<b>על פי ה'.</b> By a kiss."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:59.573206629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}